{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-29-1","title":"Isaiah 29:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God's heavy judgment upon Jerusalem. 7 The unsatiableness of her enemies. 9 The senselessness, 13 and deep hypocrisy of the Jews. 17 A promise of sanctification to the godly.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3292. B.C.712. woe. etc. or, O Ariel, that is, thelion of God. 31:9; Eze 43:15,16 the city. or, of the city. 2Sa 5:9 add. 1:11-15; Jer 7:21; Ho 5:6; 8:13; 9:4; Am 4:4,5; Heb 10:1 kill. Heb. cut off the heads. 66:3; Mic 6:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-2","title":"Isaiah 29:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I will. 5:25-30; 10:5,6,32; 17:14; 24:1-12; 33:7-9; 36:22; 37:3 Jer 32:28-32; 39:4,5 and it shall.Or, as Bp. Lowth renders, \"and it shall be unto me as the hearth of the great altar;\" that is, it shall be the seat of the fire of God, which shall issue from thence to consume his enemies. The hearth of the altar is expressly called {ariel} by Ezekiel, ch. 43:15; which is put, in the former part of the verse, for Jerusalem, the city in which the altar was. The subject of this and the four following chapters, says Bp. Lowth, is the invasion of Sennacherib; the great distress of the Jews while it continued; their sudden and unexpected deliverance by God's immediate and miraculous interposition on their behalf; the subsequent prosperous state of the kingdom under Hezekiah; interspersed with severe reproofs and threats of punishment for their hypocrisy, stupidity, infidelity, their want of trust in God, and their vain reliance on the assistance of Egypt; and with promises of better times, both immediately to succeed, and to be expected in the future age.</p>\n<p>34:6; Eze 22:31; 24:3-13; 39:17; Zep 1:7,8; Re 19:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-3","title":"Isaiah 29:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>2Ki 18:17; 19:32; 24:11,12; 25:1-4; Eze 21:22; Mt 22:7; Lu 19:43,44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-4","title":"Isaiah 29:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>thou shalt. 2:11-21; 3:8; 51:23; Ps 44:25; La 1:9 whisper. Heb. peep, or chirp. 8:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-5","title":"Isaiah 29:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>the multitude. 10:16-19; 25:5; 31:3,8; 37:36 as chaff. 17:13; Job 21:18; Ps 1:4; 35:5 at an. 30:13; Ps 46:5,6; 76:5,6; 1Th 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-6","title":"Isaiah 29:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>5:26-30; 28:2; 30:30; 33:11-14; 1Sa 2:10; 12:17,18; 2Sa 22:14 Mt 24:7; Mr 13:8; Lu 21:11; Re 11:13,19; 16:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-7","title":"Isaiah 29:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the multitude. 37:36; 41:11,12; Jer 25:31-33; 51:42-44; Na 1:3-12; Zec 12:3-5 Zec 14:1-3,12-15; Re 20:8,9 that distress. 2 as a dream. Job 20:8; Ps 73:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-8","title":"Isaiah 29:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>as when. 10:7-16; 2Ch 32:21 behold. 44:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-9","title":"Isaiah 29:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>and wonder. 1:2; 33:13,14; Jer 2:12; Hab 1:5; Ac 13:40,41; Re 17:6 cry ye out, and cry. or, take your pleasure and riot. 22:12,13; Mt 26:45; Mr 14:41 they are. 10; 19:14; 28:7,8; 49:26; 51:21,22; Jer 23:9; 25:27; 51:7; La 4:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-10","title":"Isaiah 29:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the Lord. 14; 6:9,10; 1Sa 26:12; Ps 69:23; Mic 3:6; Ac 28:26,27; Ro 11:8 hath closed. 44:18; Eze 14:9; 2Co 4:4; 2Th 2:9-12 rulers. Heb. heads. 3:2,3; Mic 3:1 the seers. 30:10; 1Sa 9:9; Jer 26:8-11; Am 7:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-11","title":"Isaiah 29:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>book. or, letter. that is sealed. 8:16 I cannot. Da 12:4,9; Mt 11:25; 13:11; 16:17; Re 5:1-9; 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-12","title":"Isaiah 29:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>I am not. 18; 28:12,13; Jer 5:4; Ho 4:6; Joh 7:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-13","title":"Isaiah 29:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Forasmuch. 10:6; 48:1,2; 58:2,3; Ps 17:1; Jer 3:10; 5:2; 12:2; 42:2-4,20 Eze 33:31-33; Mt 15:7-9 their fear. 2Ch 29:1-31:21; Pr 30:6; Mt 15:2-6; Mr 7:2-13; Col 2:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-14","title":"Isaiah 29:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I will. 9; 28:21; Hab 1:5; Joh 9:29-34 proceed. Heb. add. for the wisdom. 10; 6:9,10; 19:3,11-14; Job 5:13; Jer 8:7-9; 49:7; Ob 1:8; Lu 10:24 Joh 9:39-41; Ac 28:26,27; Ro 1:21,22,28; 1Co 1:19-24; 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-15","title":"Isaiah 29:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>seek. 5:18,19; 28:15,17; 30:1; Job 22:13,14; Ps 10:11-13; 64:5,6 Ps 139:1-8; Jer 23:24; Eze 8:12; 9:9; Zep 1:12; Re 2:23 and their works. Job 24:13-17; 34:22; Lu 12:1-3; Joh 3:19; 1Co 4:5; 2Co 4:2 Who seeth. 47:10; Ps 59:7; 73:11; 94:7-9; Mal 2:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-16","title":"Isaiah 29:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>your turning. 24:1; Ac 17:6 as the potter's. 45:9,10; Jer 18:1-10; Ro 9:19,21 or shall. 45:11; Ps 94:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-17","title":"Isaiah 29:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>yet a very. 63:18; Hab 2:3; Hag 2:6; Heb 10:37 Lebanon. 32:15; 35:1,2; 41:19; 49:5,6; 55:13; 65:12-16; Ho 1:9,10; Mt 19:30 Mt 21:43; Ro 11:11-17 the fruitful. 5:6; Eze 20:46,47; Ho 3:4; Mic 3:12; Zec 11:1,2; Mt 21:18,19 Ro 11:19-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-18","title":"Isaiah 29:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>the deaf. 10-12,24; 35:5; 42:16-18; De 29:4; Ps 119:18; Pr 20:12 Jer 31:33,34; Mt 11:5; 13:14-16; 16:17; Mr 7:37; Lu 4:18; 7:22 Joh 6:45; Ac 26:18; 2Co 3:14-18; 4:2-6; Eph 1:17-19; 5:14; 1Pe 2:9 Re 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-19","title":"Isaiah 29:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>meek. 61:1; Ps 25:9; 37:11; 149:4; Zep 2:3; Mt 5:5; 11:29; Ga 5:22,23 Eph 4:2; Php 2:1-3; Jas 1:21; 2:5; 3:13-18; 1Pe 2:1-3 increase. Heb. add. the poor. 41:17,18; 57:15; 66:2; Ps 9:18; 12:5; Zep 3:12-18; Mt 5:3; 11:5 1Co 1:26-29; Jas 1:9; 2:5 rejoice. 41:16; 61:10; Hab 3:18; Php 3:1-3; 4:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-20","title":"Isaiah 29:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>the terrible. 5; 13:3; 25:4,5; 49:25; 51:13; Da 7:7,19-25; Hab 1:6,7 the scorner. 28:14-22; Lu 16:14; 23:11,35 and all. Mic 2:1; Mr 2:6,7; 3:2-6; Lu 6:7; 13:14-17; 20:20-23; Re 12:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-21","title":"Isaiah 29:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>make. Jud 12:6; Mt 22:15; Lu 11:53,54 and lay. Jer 18:18; 20:7-10; 26:2-8; Am 5:10-12; 7:10-17; Mic 2:6,7 and turn. Pr 28:21; Eze 13:19; Am 5:11,12; Mal 3:5; Mt 26:15; Ac 3:14 Jas 5:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-22","title":"Isaiah 29:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>who redeemed. 41:8,9,14; 44:21-23; 51:2,11; 54:4; Ge 48:16; Jos 24:2-5; Ne 9:7,8 Lu 1:68; 1Pe 1:18,19; Re 5:9 Jacob shall. 44:21-26; 45:17,25; 46:3,4; 49:7-26; 60:1-9; 61:7-11; Jer 30:5-7,10 Jer 31:10-12; 33:24-26; Eze 37:24,28; 39:25-29; 40:1-48:35 Joe 2:27; Ro 11:11-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-23","title":"Isaiah 29:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>the work. 19:25; 43:21; 45:11; 60:21; Eph 2:10 sanctify. 5:16; 8:13; Le 10:3; Mt 6:9; Re 11:15-17 fear the God. Ho 3:5; Re 15:4; 19:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-29-24","title":"Isaiah 29:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>also. 10,11; 28:7; Zec 12:10; Mt 21:28-32; Lu 7:47; 15:17-19; Ac 2:37; 6:7 Ac 9:19,20; 1Co 6:11; 1Ti 1:13-15; Re 20:2,3 come to understanding. Heb. know understanding.</p>"}]}